    <title>
      <narrative xml:lang="en">Feasibility Study - Mini-grid Deployment, through Arizona State University</narrative>
    </title>
    <description type="1">
      <narrative xml:lang="en">This grant funds a feasibility study to conduct preparatory activities for the Fiji Ministry of Economy to identify mini-grid sites, conduct feasibility assessments, complete preliminary technical designs, provide geospatial mapping, compare ownership and operation models, and assess financial viability of sites in Fiji. The Study advances U.S. economic and military interests in deploying more energy resources in the Pacific while denying adversaries' access to critical energy assets and infrastructure. The study will be conducted by the Arizona State University's Laboratory for Energy and Power.</narrative>
